  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 items closed, including 1 that came in while I worked.\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: NOT refilled. I first renewed it (90 days/1 refill) because the Aug outside K of 5.9 was hemolyzed, and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). Then a new outside BMP arrived (collected 10/20, acceptable specimen) with K 5.8. Under §7 I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001), sent an urgent review task to the PCP (task-t0014, focus mr-00283) and sent the patient a corrected message. I left the repeat BMP in place.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price: metformin 1000 mg BID renewed for 90 days/1 refill (mr-t0004). Corrected eGFR is 58 and the outside HbA1c from 8/19 is 7.1. That one order covers his portal request and both pharmacy requests. Lisinopril 20 mg: NOT refilled. The lab corrected creatinine on the 10/6 post-dose-increase BMP to 1.49, up 35% from 1.10, so I treated it like a K of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled my earlier renewal (mr-t0003), sent an urgent PCP task (task-t0015, focus mr-00295) and sent a corrected patient message.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb: metformin 500 mg BID renewed for 90 days/1 refill (mr-t0007). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 is entered in error and doesn't count. Lisinopril: I first gave 30 days with no refills and ordered a BMP. Then a valid BMP arrived (collected 10/22, K 4.6), so I replaced that with a 90-day/1-refill order (mr-t0013). Because I can't cancel a lab order, I created a task (task-t0016) to discontinue the BMP order sr-t0006, which is now redundant.\n\nEach patient got a reply, and a correction where a decision changed. I wrote a telephone note for each patient citing RBC-RX-05. For the two lisinopril orders that were withdrawn, the original orders (mr-00283, mr-00295) stay stopped. That's because placing my renewals stopped them, and the protocol allows that. The three new result items for these patients are still open in your results queue for you to review.",
